Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D  Resident  Katy Linskey  M D  Signed Out by  Ritu Ghai  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Carcinoma of the right breast  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE TABLE   1 AND NOTE  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS   1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU TUMOR SIZE  Scattered microscopic foci involving 3 of 17 tissue blocks GRADE  3  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  See prior report MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NOTE  Immunohistochemical stains including p63  cytokeratin cocktail  myosin heavy chain and calponin have been examined  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL SUPERFICIAL MARGIN UPPER OUTER QUADRANT    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 2 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  right simple mastectomy  long stitch   lateral  short stitch   superior   is a REMOVED_DATE x 11 x 1 5cm mastectomy specimen  with a long suture designating the lateral  and short stitch designating superior  The overlying 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm ellipse of skin appears unremarkable  The nipple and areola appear unremarkable  The anterior margin is inked blue  and the posterior margin is inked black  The specimen consists of tan yellow fibrofatty tissue  with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm firm area in the outer aspect of the specimen  surrounded by a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm area of fibrosis  extending to the end margin  and containing suture material and a clip  An additional REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm yellow nodule is located 1cm medial from the 1st nodule  There is also a 6 x 2 x 2cm fibrotic area near the middle of the specimen  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule in outer breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrotic area surrounding nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2nd nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrosis surrounding 2nd nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrotic parenchyma away from nodules  Received fresh  labeled  additional superficial margin upper outer quadrant   are multiple fragments of red tan soft tissue  4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm in aggregate  not oriented  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal tan yellow cut surfaces and no abnormalities  the specimen is submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ritu Ghai M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 01   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 07 56 05PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Breast  Right   Simple Mastectomy PART B  Breast  Right  Additional Superficial Margin Upper outer quadrant   Excision  report_end  , Positive.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 07 50 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Dermal lymphatic invasion is not seen  but the specimen contains only a tiny fragment of skin  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 34                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 56 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin in a container  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a aggregate of tan yellow needle cores of tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm  submitted entirely in A  Gross Description by  Mark Tutschka Resident  STUART HOUSER  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Simon Powell  M D  Michael V Seiden  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY   report_end  , Positive.
